{
  "title": "Scheduler — Overview",
  "uid": "scheduler-overview",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "timezone": "browser",
  "time": { "from": "now-1h", "to": "now" },
  "refresh": "10s",
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Service up",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": { "h": 4, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [{ "expr": "up{job=\"scheduler-api\"}", "refId": "A" }]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Process CPU (rate)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "rate(process_cpu_seconds_total{job=\"scheduler-api\"}[5m])", "refId": "A" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Heap used (bytes)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 0 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        { "expr": "nodejs_heap_size_used_bytes{job=\"scheduler-api\"}", "refId": "A" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Event loop lag (p99, seconds)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 8 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "nodejs_eventloop_lag_p99_seconds{job=\"scheduler-api\"}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Deferred — booking domain panels",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 8 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Not built yet.** Once the scheduler domain exposes its own counters (booking success/conflict rate, availability-check latency, idempotency replay rate — see `docs/09_devops_infrastructure.md`), add panels here rather than a new dashboard. This is the seam, not a placeholder for its own sake."
      }
    }
  ]
}
